/-!
# A native exchange of the two first-class involutions in census pair 10

The displayed word interchanges the literal source central involution and
source representative 10. Packed products verify the word and both
intertwining identities in the faithful 112-dimensional matrix representation.
Thus the exchange takes place in J4 itself. It will transport both full
centralizer residuals, without a test for membership in a smaller two-core.

Source: Kleidman--Wilson (1988), pp.485,487, the transitivity on involutions
of each class in a four-group and Corollary 1.1.4. Matrix and word attribution
remain those of LocalInvolutionCensus/Fusion/source/README.md (ATLAS).
-/

